---
/**
 * A decoy field. Hidden from sight and from screen readers, and skipped by
 * keyboard navigation, so no real visitor can fill it in — but a bot parsing
 * the HTML sees an ordinary text input and completes it.
 *
 * The API drops any submission that arrives with `website` set, and answers
 * with a normal success response so the bot doesn't learn to omit it. See
 * HONEYPOT_FIELDS in cedar-grove-api's src/lib/formGuard.ts.
 *
 * All four forms serialize with FormData, so this is picked up automatically
 * with no change to their submit handlers.
 */
---

<div class="hp-field" aria-hidden="true">
  <label for="website">Website</label>
  <input type="text" id="website" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
</div>

<style>
  /* Not `display: none` or `hidden`: some bots skip fields hidden that
     obviously. Positioned off-screen instead, which is invisible in exactly
     the same way to a person but still looks like a live field in the DOM. */
  .hp-field {
    position: absolute;
    left: -9999px;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
</style>
